(
    id: "deadman_relay",
    name: "Deadman Relay",
    description: "Scavenged module. Wintermute's own switch, cut out of the wreck and wired to the party bus.",
    // The second item to grant a routine that already ships, and the louder
    // case: `deadman` is `exclusive`, an Everyone-scope routine three times
    // `core_dump`'s power, and until now reachable only by beating
    // Wintermute for the disk. This is still that — the relay drops from
    // Wintermute and nothing else — but it spends a module slot rather than
    // a routine slot, and unlike the disk it cannot be etched or taught on.
    // Exclusivity was never about how many things can carry a routine; it is
    // about the routine never entering `KnownRoutines`, and a grant is
    // derived off the worn item rather than learned.
    value: Some(180),
    equipment: Some((Module, (mitigation: 6))),
    grants: Some("deadman"),
    droppable: Some([("wintermute", 0.12)]),
)
